    "author": "@abbyr654",
    "text": "picsmics4, you and i have an eerily similar story. i'm probably your age, and also experienced A LOT of trauma in the last 10 years after college. I lost so many family members, lost most of my friends, dove into drug addiction, was homeless, estranged from my family, hopping jobs... It's hard to keep going when you've lost so much, and all of your best memories are behind you. Yet somehow, you keep moving forward with this video as a kind of North Star to guide you.  It's something all of us can learn from: we are never too old to find enjoyment in the things we love.\n\nYou don't need another commenter telling you they're rooting for you - so I'll just tell you that you're truly not alone. It gives a lot of us hope that you continue on your path and come back to the thing that makes you happy. Maybe more of us will start doing the same. Thank you for sharing your life with us and showing the rest of us that it's okay to love what you love.",
    "time": "2 years ago"
