  {
    "author": "@zack2920",
    "text": "Here I am, on a sleepless night kind of like picsmics4, commenting on this video. \n\nI have JUST heard your story for the first time today, and had to pay a visit here. I don’t know you, I likely never will, but I’m sitting here overwhelmed by some melancholy, wistful feeling while listening to this video, knowing it was the soundtrack to so many formative moments for you, so many sleepless nights of your own. It’s an avenue for you to connect to those nostalgic, carefree days. It isn’t that for me, but I’m oddly overwhelmed by it. I struggle with empathy at times, and yet I feel it deeply in this moment, for some reason, knowing how often you heard it and how ingrained in your brain it must be.\n\nMy life is good right now. At times, it hasn’t been. You and I are probably around the same age, and it’s humbling to consider my own highs and lows since your first comment. I’m thinking of people I’ve lost, new people that are now central to my life, knowing some of them may not be in another 15 years, and knowing people I haven’t met yet will be there, if I am, god willing. \n\nLooking back on your original comments from so many years ago, I remember talking like that to my friends and to strangers in almost empty comment sections just like this one used to be. That, by itself, has connected me to those memories of my own in a way that I haven’t in so long. It’s a really good feeling. Thank you for that. \n\nI hope you’re happy, stranger. I hope you’re finding the time to create happiness for yourself. I’m happy for you that, despite your trials, you have endured and overcome to the extent that you have. \n\nI’m glad the echoes echoed back for you. ❤️",
    "time": "2 years ago (edited)"
  },
