    "author": "@cesarramos9766",
    "text": "Just read the story of this entire video and picmics's comments and I genuinely cried a bit. \n\nI do relate to him when it comes to vehemently seek comfort when life gives you nothing but adversity and problems, but you still decide not to give up, no matter how tired, desperate and unhopeful you feel. I've been battling against depression since I hit puberty and since then I've had a rough time finding happiness and a taste for life. I've cried, screamed, cursed and vehemently asked for God to end my life because I feel like my life is a whole torture I've been through four suicide attempts and I'm still alive. Thank God I'm finally seeking therapy and have grown up as a person to say I'm better than yesterday. I'm really fighting for myself against my mind and adversity. Those who battle and carry on with life despite the number of obstacles and adversities are the strongest people ever.",
    "time": "2 years ago (edited)"
